# Rule Engine Architecture

## Overview
The Rule Engine is a core component of the timesheet microservice that evaluates business rules for timesheet calculations. It follows a strategy pattern with support for both duration-based and range-based rule evaluation.

## Core Components

### Main Interfaces
- [IRuleEngine.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/IRuleEngine.java) - Main rule engine interface
- [IRuleFactory.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/IRuleFactory.java) - Rule factory interface for creating rule instances

### Core Implementation
- [RuleEngine.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/RuleEngine.java) - Main rule engine implementation
- [RuleFactory.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/RuleFactory.java) - Factory implementation for creating rules

### Evaluation Strategies
- [RuleEvaluationStrategy.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/RuleEvaluationStrategy.java) - Base strategy interface
- [DurationBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/DurationBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy.java) - Strategy for duration-based rules
- [RangeBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/RangeBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy.java) - Strategy for range-based rules

### Configuration
- [RuleEngineConfiguration.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/RuleEngineConfiguration.java) - Spring configuration for rule engine beans

### Controllers
- [IRuleEngineController.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/IRuleEngineController.java) - Controller interface
- [RuleEngineController.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/RuleEngineController.java) - REST controller implementation

