```

## Usage Patterns

### Rule Engine Service Integration
```java
@Service
public class RuleEngineService {
    
    private final IRuleEngine ruleEngine;
    private final RuleEngineMapper ruleEngineMapper;
    
    public RuleValidationResult validateTimesheetRules(Timesheet timesheet) {
        // Convert timesheet to rule engine format
        RuleEngineInputDto input = ruleEngineMapper.toRuleEngineInput(timesheet);
        
        // Execute rules
        RuleEngineResult result = ruleEngine.evaluateRules(input);
        
        // Convert result
        return ruleEngineMapper.toValidationResult(result);
    }
}
```

### Rule Factory Usage
```java
@Component
public class RuleFactory {
    
    public IEvaluatableRule createRule(RuleType ruleType, RuleConfiguration config) {
        // Factory logic to create appropriate rule instance
        return ruleFactory.createRule(ruleType, config);
    }
}
```

### Evaluation Strategy Pattern
```java
// Duration-based evaluation
DurationBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy durationStrategy = 
    new DurationBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy();
RuleResult result = durationStrategy.evaluate(rule, timeLogs);

// Range-based evaluation
RangeBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy rangeStrategy = 
    new RangeBasedRuleEvaluationStrategy();
RuleResult result = rangeStrategy.evaluate(rule, timeRanges);
```

## Testing Patterns

### Rule Engine Service Tests
```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class RuleEngineServiceTests {
    
    @Mock
    private IRuleEngine ruleEngine;
    
    @Mock
    private RuleEngineMapper ruleEngineMapper;
    
    @Test
    void testEvaluateRulesSuccess() {
        // Arrange
        given(this.ruleEngine.evaluateRules(any())).willReturn(result);
        given(this.ruleEngineMapper.toRuleEngineResponseBodyDto(any())).willReturn(responseDto);
        
        // Act
        RuleEngineResponseBodyDto result = this.ruleEngineService.evaluateRules(requestDto);
        
        // Assert
        assertThat(result).isEqualTo(expectedResponse);
        verify(this.ruleEngine).evaluateRules(any());
    }
}
```

## Default Pay (Week-end Sweep)

A virtual/system rule that pays any worked time still unallocated after all daily rules and Weekly Overtime have run. Adds two RuleType values:

- `RANGE_BASED_DEFAULT_PAY` (id 13)
- `DURATION_BASED_DEFAULT_PAY` (id 14)

Gated per timesheet on `TimesheetSetting.isUnplannedHoursPayEnabled == 1`. Sits last in `RulePrecedenceConfig` for both range-based and duration-based lists, but is dispatched **outside the per-rule daily loop** — invoked at week end by `BaseRuleEvaluator.evaluateDefaultPayRules` after `evaluateWeeklyOvertimeRules`. See [DefaultPayRule.md](mdc:.cursor/rules/DefaultPayRule.md) for the chronological-backfill algorithm and the WOT interaction.

The two rule classes are:
- [shifts/DefaultPayRule.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/rules/shifts/DefaultPayRule.java)
- [hourly/DefaultPayRule.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/rule_engine/rules/hourly/DefaultPayRule.java)

Both compute `duration × baseRate × 1.0` via `TimeHelper.calculatePayAmount` / `calculateBillAmount` with `ChargeMethodType.MULTIPLIER`.

## Best Practices

### Rule Implementation
- Extend appropriate base classes for rule types
- Use strategy pattern for different evaluation approaches
- Implement proper validation in rule constructors
- Use builder pattern for complex rule configurations

### Performance Considerations
- Use caching for frequently accessed rule configurations
- Implement bulk evaluation for multiple timesheets
- Use appropriate evaluation strategies based on rule type
- Optimize rule matching algorithms

### Error Handling
- Provide meaningful error messages for rule violations
- Use custom exceptions for rule-specific errors
- Implement proper logging for rule evaluation
- Handle edge cases in rule calculations

